  "summary": "One frozen, typed set of M5 breakpoint specs and mapping-state pills. Every breakpoint carries one canonical pill that pins one verification state (pending, verified, unbound, unsupported, policy-blocked) and one mapping state (exact, misaligned, needs-remap, unmapped), so a breakpoint shown in a gutter, session header, list, notebook cell, replay timeline, or export packet traces back to one spec and one state vocabulary. A green confirmed-stop icon renders only when a breakpoint is verified, exact, and not replay-only; an unbound, misaligned, replay-only, or policy-blocked breakpoint always discloses. Breakpoint identity survives rename, reformat, and import where a stable logical source identity exists, and degrades to an explicit needs-remap rather than vanishing when it does not; a lexical fallback is never presented as an exact semantic mapping; and notebook and replay views keep stable cell and frame identity.",
